<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2014/Treeline.jpg" alt="A painting of bushes in a treeline. This uses transparent darks and an impressionistic foreground with texture effects." width="500" height="367" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Treeline. 9x12, oil on linen panel. 2014</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I started this painting on location at Riverside Potomac Farm in Lucketts, VA. By the time I have completed the block-in I was cold and it was just about to start raining. I packed up my gear and headed home, where I finished the painting in my studio.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The bushes at the focal point of the painting were actually the hardest part to get right: I scraped that area back and repainted it a couple of times. I kept the feel of a plein air painting by allowing myself the same amount of time to work on it in the studio that I would have had out in the field (with a little extra time added for scraping and re-painting).&nbsp;</p>